- DefinePartitionKey: defines the partition key', example='Rename'),
      ruleExpression?: string(name='RuleExpression', description='The rule expression in JSON string format.


Example of a rename rule (Rename):
{"expression":"${srcDatasourceName}_${srcDatabaseName}_0922","variables":[{"variableName":"srcDatabaseName","variableRules":[{"from":"fromdb","to":"todb"}]}]}
- expression: the expression for the rename transformation rule. Supported variables in the expression include ${srcDatasourceName} (source data source name), ${srcDatabaseName} (source database name), and ${srcTableName} (source table name).
- variables: the generation rules for each variable in the rename transformation rule expression. The default value of a parameter is the original value of the corresponding meaning at the source. You can define a set of string replacement rules to rewrite the original value as needed. variableName: the variable name, excluding the ${} characters. variableRules: the variable generation rule group. Replacements are performed in sequential execution. from: the original string. to: the replaced string.


Example of a rule to add a specified column and assign a value at the destination (AddColumn):
{"columns":[{"columnName":"my_add_column","columnValueType":"Constant","columnValue":"123"}]}
- If not specified, the default rule is that no columns are added and no replication is performed.
- columnName: the name of the appended column.
- columnValueType: the value type of the appended column. Valid values: Constant (constant) and Variable (variable).
- columnValue: the value of the appended column. When valueType is Constant, value is a custom constant of the String type. When valueType is Variable, value is a built-in variable. Valid values for built-in variables include EXECUTE_TIME (execution time, Long type), DB_NAME_SRC (source database name, String type), DATASOURCE_NAME_SRC (source data source name, String type), TABLE_NAME_SRC (source table name, String type), DB_NAME_DEST (destination database name, String type), DATASOURCE_NAME_DEST (destination data source name, String type), TABLE_NAME_DEST (destination table name, String type), and DB_NAME_SRC_TRANSED (transformed database name, String type).

Example of specifying the primary key column names for the destination table (DefinePrimaryKey):
{"columns":["ukcolumn1","ukcolumn2"]}
- If not specified, the source primary key columns are used by default.
- When the destination is an existing table: the data integration system does not modify the destination table schema. If the specified primary key columns are not in the column set of the destination, an error is reported when the task starts.
- When the destination is an automatically created table: the data integration system automatically creates the destination table schema, and the table schema includes the defined primary key columns. If the specified primary key columns are not in the column set of the destination, an error is reported when the task starts.

Example of a DML handling rule (HandleDml):
{"dmlPolicies":[{"dmlType":"Delete","dmlAction":"Filter","filterCondition":"id > 1"}]}
- If not specified, the default rule is Normal for Insert, Update, and Delete.
- dmlType: the DML operations type. Valid values: Insert (insert), Update (update), and Delete (delete).
- dmlAction: the DML handling policy. Valid values: Normal (normal handling), Ignore (ignore), Filter (conditional normal handling, used when dmlType is Update or Delete), and LogicalDelete (logical delete).
- filterCondition: the DML filter condition, used when dmlAction is Filter.', example='{"expression":"${srcDatasoureName}_${srcDatabaseName}"}'),
