  content?: string(name='Content', description='The code content of the file. The code format varies based on the file type. You can go to Operation Center, right-click a task of the corresponding type, and select View Code to view the specific code format.', example='SELECT "1";'),
  cronExpress?: string(name='CronExpress', description='The cron expression for periodic scheduling. This parameter corresponds to the Cron Expression parameter in the Schedule > Time Property > Cron Expression section of the [DataWorks console](https://workbench.data.aliyun.com/console). After you configure the scheduling cycle and scheduled time, DataWorks automatically generates the corresponding cron expression.

Examples:

- Schedule a node at 05:30 every day: `00 30 05 * * ?`.

- Schedule a node at the 15th minute of every hour: `00 15 * * * ?`.

- Schedule a node every 10 minutes: `00 00/10 * * * ?`.

- Schedule a node every 10 minutes from 08:00 to 17:00 every day: `00 00-59/10 8-23 * * * ?`.

- Schedule a node at 00:20 on the first day of every month: `00 20 00 1 * ?`.

- Schedule a node every three months starting from 00:10 on January 1: `00 10 00 1 1-12/3 ?`.

- Schedule a node at 00:05 every Tuesday and Friday: `00 05 00 * * 2,5`.

Due to the rules of the DataWorks scheduling system, cron expressions have the following limits:

- The minimum scheduling interval is 5 minutes.

- The earliest scheduling time of a day is 00:05.', example='00 00-59/5 1-23 * * ?'),
  cycleType?: string(name='CycleType', description='The type of the scheduling cycle. Valid values: NOT_DAY (minute and hour) and DAY (day, week, and month).

